# Shell — Pre-approved (npm, pip, npx)

For **this repository**, the agent may run npm, pip, and npx commands without asking for permission first. Git and `gh` are covered separately in `.cursor/rules/git-allowed.mdc`.

## npm (allowed)

Run npm directly for dependency and script workflows:

- `npm install`, `npm ci`, `npm update`, `npm uninstall` (when changing dependencies as part of the task)
- `npm run` (any script defined in `package.json`)
- `npm test`, `npm exec`, `npm run test`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, etc.
- `npx` (see below)

## pip / Python (allowed)

Run pip for Python dependency and tooling workflows:

- `pip install`, `pip install -r requirements.txt`, `pip uninstall` (when changing dependencies as part of the task)
- `python3 -m pip install`, `python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt`, and other `python3 -m pip` subcommands
- `python3 -m pytest`, `python3 -m unittest`, and similar module invocations when running tests or scripts

## npx / Node.js tooling (allowed)

Use `npx` to invoke Node.js CLI tools without a global install:

- `npx vitest`, `npx playwright`, `npx vite`, `npx eslint`, `npx prettier`, and similar project tooling
- Any `npx` command that runs a dev, test, build, or lint tool for this repo

## Guardrails (still apply)

- Do **not** run delete/remove commands (`rm`, `git clean`, `docker compose down -v`, `docker rm`, etc.) unless the user explicitly requests them.
- Do **not** run destructive system or container commands unless the user explicitly requests them.
- Prefer repo scripts (`npm run …`) when they exist instead of ad-hoc equivalents.
